def button
  title "Push button to ground with a pull-up"
  about "A push button pulls a signal to ground; a 10 kΩ pull-up holds it high while the button is open, also before
      the firmware runs. Without the resistor the MCU's internal pull-up does the job once the firmware has set it."
  port in "the signal to the MCU input"
  port vcc "the logic supply of that input (3.3 V or 5 V)"
  port gnd "ground"
  part SW1 button TS-1187A-B-A-B lcsc C318884 "{as}: push button"
    nc B D
    notes "Pins 1/2 and 3/4 are connected inside."
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: pull-up 10 k"
  net in @vcc SW1.A R1.2
  net vcc R1.1
  net gnd SW1.C
  covers LVL.undefined HINT.debounce
  notes "Debounce in the firmware (hint HINT.debounce)."
  notes "sim.json: the net under the MCU's inputs; the button under buttons in one load, so that LVL.threshold sees
      both levels."
  notes "On a strapping pin the pull-up must agree with the boot level (LVL.boot)."
